2026-02-10T05:43:42.092645Z  INFO session_loop{thread_id=019c45c9-8c4e-7503-a2c1-503a7ea82ca9}: codex_core::stream_events_utils: ToolCall: exec_command {"cmd":"cat <<'EOF' > .specify/checklists/requirements.md\n# Requirements Quality Checklist: Use Case Flow Specification\n\n**Purpose**: Validate clarity, completeness, and consistency of requirements in spec.md and plan.md\n**Created**: 2026-02-10\n**Feature**: .specify/spec.md\n\n**Note**: This checklist is generated by the `/speckit.checklist` command based on feature context and requirements.\n\n## Requirement Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK001 Are all user stories mapped to explicit functional requirements? [Traceability, Spec §User Scenarios, Spec §FR-001–FR-040]\n- [ ] CHK002 Are out-of-scope items explicitly documented to prevent scope creep? [Gap]\n- [ ] CHK003 Are required paper metadata fields explicitly specified? [Gap, Spec §FR-015]\n- [ ] CHK004 Are manuscript file format and size limits explicitly specified? [Gap, Spec §FR-016]\n- [ ] CHK005 Are required review fields explicitly specified? [Gap, Spec §FR-029]\n- [ ] CHK006 Are attendance types explicitly enumerated or constrained? [Gap, Spec §FR-039]\n\n## Requirement Clarity\n\n- [ ] CHK007 Is \"password complexity\" defined with concrete rules (e.g., character classes)? [Ambiguity, Spec §FR-003, Spec §FR-012]\n- [ ] CHK008 Is \"invalid draft information\" defined with specific validation rules? [Ambiguity, Spec §FR-019]\n- [ ] CHK009 Is \"standard conference size\" in scheduling performance defined with measurable bounds? [Ambiguity, Spec §SC-004]\n- [ ] CHK010 Is the retention period anchored to a precise \"conference end date\" definition? [Ambiguity, Spec §FR-040]\n\n## Requirement Consistency\n\n- [ ] CHK011 Are username and email uniqueness rules consistent across registration and login flows? [Consistency, Spec §FR-002, Spec §FR-007]\n- [ ] CHK012 Do role constraints in the flows align with all role-based requirements? [Consistency, Spec §User Scenarios, Spec §FR-021–FR-033]\n- [ ] CHK013 Is the tech stack in plan.md consistent with constitution constraints (C++ and style guide)? [Consistency, Plan §Technical Context, Constitution]\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK014 Are all success criteria measurable and verifiable without implementation details? [Measurability, Spec §SC-001–SC-005]\n- [ ] CHK015 Are success criteria defined for each major workflow area (auth, submissions, reviews, scheduling, registration)? [Completeness, Spec §SC-001–SC-005]\n\n## Scenario Coverage\n\n- [ ] CHK016 Are alternate flows for all user stories captured in requirements (not only in narratives)? [Coverage, Spec §User Scenarios]\n- [ ] CHK017 Are notification requirements (channel, timing) explicitly specified for all flows that notify users? [Gap, Spec §FR-025, Spec §FR-033, Spec §FR-038]\n- [ ] CHK018 Are requirements defined for unauthorized access attempts across all protected flows? [Coverage, Spec §User Scenarios]\n\n## Edge Case Coverage\n\n- [ ] CHK019 Are duplicate submission rules defined for drafts, reviews, and decisions beyond the stated examples? [Coverage, Spec §Edge Cases]\n- [ ] CHK020 Are conflict resolution rules specified for concurrent schedule edits? [Gap, Spec §FR-036]\n- [ ] CHK021 Are retry/rollback requirements specified for system errors during save operations? [Gap, Spec §Edge Cases]\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- [ ] CHK022 Are performance targets defined for authentication and submission flows in addition to scheduling? [Gap, Spec §SC-001–SC-004]\n- [ ] CHK023 Are availability/recovery expectations defined for the CMS (uptime, restore targets)? [Gap]\n- [ ] CHK024 Are privacy handling requirements specified for data deletion after retention ends? [Gap, Spec §FR-040]\n\n## Dependencies & Assumptions\n\n- [ ] CHK025 Are external dependencies (payment service, email delivery) specified with failure handling requirements? [Gap, Spec §User Story 12, Spec §User Story 1, Spec §User Story 6]\n- [ ] CHK026 Are assumptions about rooms/time slots and registration state explicitly linked to requirements? [Clarity, Spec §Assumptions & Dependencies]\n\n## Ambiguities & Conflicts\n\n- [ ] CHK027 Are any requirements using terms like \"valid\" or \"invalid\" without definition? [Ambiguity, Spec §FR-015, Spec §FR-019, Spec §FR-029]\n- [ ] CHK028 Is there an explicit requirement/acceptance mapping for UAT items to FRs? [Traceability, Spec §UAT]\n\n## Notes\n\n- Check items off as completed: `[x]`\n- Add comments or findings inline\n- Items are numbered sequentially for easy reference\nEOF"} thread_id=019c45c9-8c4e-7503-a2c1-503a7ea82ca9
